      "claim": "The concept of 'fair trade' implies voluntary exchange, market competition, and equitable pricing mechanisms between independent agents.",
      "evidence": "Modern definitions of fair trade and standard economic ethics rely on the freedom of parties to enter or exit contracts and on prices reflecting supply and demand, rather than fixed, coercive dues.",
